  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has a sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. Let's call a contiguous subsequence of AAA a segment.\n\nA segment is good if it can be divided into at most KKK segments such that the sum of elements in each of these sub-segments is at most SSS.\n\nYou need to find the maximum number of elements in a good segment.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains three space-separated integers NNN, KKK and SSS.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer — the maximum length of a good segment.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤150,0001 \\le T \\le 150,0001≤T≤150,000",
      "1≤K≤N≤1051 \\le K \\le N \\le 10^51≤K≤N≤105",
      "1≤S≤1091 \\le S \\le 10^91≤S≤109",
      "1≤Ai≤S1 \\le A_i \\le S1≤Ai​≤S for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10610^6106",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask #1 (100 points):** original constraints"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n5 2 5\n1 3 2 1 5\n5 3 5\n5 1 5 1 1",
        "output": "4\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: One of the segments with length 444 is [1,3,2,1][1, 3, 2, 1][1,3,2,1]. It can be divided into two segments [1,3][1, 3][1,3] and [2,1][2, 1][2,1] whose sums are at most S=5S = 5S=5."
      }
    ]
  },
